      "{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Is there a free AI wardrobe designer?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes. ChatGPT and Google Gemini are free and useful for fashion recommendations. FitWardrobe will be free during early access, with AI tagging and outfit suggestions, but it is not available yet.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can AI design my outfits?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"AI can suggest outfit combinations from your existing wardrobe based on colour theory, occasion, and style matching. Wardrobe apps such as FitWardrobe (coming soon) generate these suggestions from what you own. For more creative or aspirational styling, ChatGPT can provide detailed personalised advice.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the best free wardrobe app?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"For Android users prioritising privacy: FitWardrobe once it launches (free during early access, wardrobe stored on your device, cloud AI). For iOS or Android users who want something now: Acloset's free tier (up to 100 items, listed limit, October 2026) and Whering are starting points. See our full app comparison for detailed reviews.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Is it safe to upload my wardrobe to an AI app?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"It depends on the app. Many free apps upload photos to cloud servers. FitWardrobe (coming soon) stores your wardrobe on your device, but photos are sent to a cloud AI service when you ask for tags or suggestions. Always check an app's privacy policy before sharing personal images.\"}}]}",
