      "{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Is there an app that helps you put together outfits for free?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes, many apps offer free versions. FitWardrobe, coming soon on Android and the web, will be free during early access.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How do I use an outfit app effectively?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Start small by digitizing your most-worn items. Use the app to plan your outfits the night before to save time in the morning. If your app has wear statistics (or you keep a wear log), review them to declutter items you don't use.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can apps really style me better than I can?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Apps can provide a fresh perspective. AI algorithms don't have \\\"habit bias,\\\" so they might suggest color combinations or layering options you simply haven't considered, helping you expand your style potential.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Is it worth cataloging every item or just the ones you wear most?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Catalog everything. The items you wear least are often the most important to have in the system — the AI can surface forgotten pieces that pair well with items you wear constantly, creating new outfit combinations you wouldn't have discovered otherwise. A partial catalogue produces partial insights.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How do outfit planning apps handle formal or ethnic wear that's worn rarely?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"In apps that support occasion or formality tags, tag occasion wear accurately (wedding, formal, festival) so it comes up when you ask for that kind of outfit rather than crowding everyday suggestions. In FitWardrobe, you ask for outfits by occasion, and suggestions only use clothes you own.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What's the difference between outfit planning and just knowing your wardrobe well?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Knowledge of your wardrobe is passive. Outfit planning is active — it commits to specific combinations, builds a searchable library of what's worked, and tracks the data that updates your knowledge over time. People who \\\"know their wardrobe well\\\" may discover, when they catalogue it, that their knowledge was out of date or incomplete.\"}}]}",
